{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Records are anonymous bytes in a section, and the linker concatenates them, so two modules can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"register the same route or the same event name, and nothing notices until the program reads the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set. The linker does refuse two definitions of one symbol. A record declared with a unique key gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a function beside it whose symbol is named for the record’s kind and the key, so a second","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration of that kind and key defines the symbol again and the build fails, naming it.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574, uniqueKey: \"\/home\")","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/home\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the key as a string literal. A client’s own macro gives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each declaration its key from LinkerSetsMacroSupport’s "},{"code":"uniqueKey(of:attribute:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration, such as an event type’s name, or from an argument of the attribute through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"uniqueKeyArgument(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Records of different kinds never clash, because the kind is part of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbol’s name."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What the developer sees","anchor":"What-the-developer-sees"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$linkerset_kind_<kind>_key_<key>"},{"type":"text","text":": the kind as eight hex digits, then the key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with ASCII letters and digits as they are and every other UTF-8 byte as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_"},{"type":"text","text":" and two hex digits. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"route above is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$linkerset_kind_726F7574_key__2Fhome"},{"type":"text","text":", and an event named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrderPlaced"},{"type":"text","text":" of kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"evnt\""},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two declarations in one module are caught by the compiler:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["error: multiple definitions of symbol '$linkerset_kind_726F7574_key__2Fhome'"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two modules linked into one program are caught by the linker, which names both object files. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"linker words it its own way."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apple’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["duplicate symbol '_$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced' in:","    ...\/libCheckout.a[2](OrderPlaced.swift.o)","    ...\/libOrders.a[2](OrderPlaced.swift.o)","ld: 1 duplicate symbols"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"LLVM’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"lld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ELF, which Bazel links with on Linux and Android uses, points at the macro","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expansion that declares each one:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["ld.lld: error: duplicate symbol: $linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced",">>> defined at @__swiftmacro_6Orders11OrderPlaced5EventfMp_.swift:6",">>>            OrderPlaced.swift.o:($linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced) in archive libOrders.a",">>> defined at @__swiftmacro_8Checkout11OrderPlaced5EventfMp_.swift:6",">>>            OrderPlaced.swift.o:(.text.$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced+0x0) in archive libCheckout.a"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GNU gold, which "},{"code":"swiftc","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" links with on Linux by default:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["\/usr\/bin\/ld.gold: error: .\/libCheckout.a(OrderPlaced.swift.o): multiple definition of '$linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced'","\/usr\/bin\/ld.gold: .\/libOrders.a(OrderPlaced.swift.o): previous definition here"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"wasm-ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", for WebAssembly:"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["wasm-ld: error: duplicate symbol: $linkerset_kind_65766E74_key_OrderPlaced",">>> defined in ...\/Orders.objlib\/a.o",">>> defined in ...\/Checkout.objlib\/b.o"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Windows, "},{"code":"lld-link","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"link.exe","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" refuse a symbol defined twice as well ("},{"code":"LNK2005","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"link.exe","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), but no test shows it yet."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"One linked image at a time","anchor":"One-linked-image-at-a-time"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The check covers the modules linked statically into one executable or one shared library. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t reach across images:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Shared libraries and frameworks keep their symbols apart. On Apple platforms each image’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbols live in a namespace of their own, and on ELF the first definition the loader finds wins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without an error. The function is internal, so a library doesn’t export it either.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A library opened with ","type":"text"},{"code":"dlopen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never compared with the program.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record of the same key in another image is still read, so a client that needs the guarantee for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the whole process keeps a check at run time too, such as throwing when two records share a name."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Static archives","anchor":"Static-archives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A static archive’s member is linked only when something references it. Its record and its key’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"symbol sit in the same object file, so the two are linked together or not at all: a module whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records are missing (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"reference"},{"text":") is missing from the check as well.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftPM and Bazel link a target’s modules whole, and there a duplicate is an error. Apple’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes one exception: with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-dead_strip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the default for release builds in Xcode, a duplicate from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an archive member read on demand is only a warning, ","type":"text"},{"code":"ld: warning: duplicate symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the link","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"succeeds. Link the archive whole (","type":"text"},{"code":"-force_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"-all_load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for every archive), or make the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"linker’s warnings errors with ","type":"text"},{"code":"-Xlinker -fatal_warnings","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", to keep it an error. Linux’s linkers and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"wasm-ld","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" make it an error either way.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Where a key can’t be checked","anchor":"Where-a-key-cant-be-checked"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A symbol declared inside a ","type":"text"},{"code":"private","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"fileprivate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, or an extension marked either way, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"local to its file, and the linker never compares local symbols. The macros refuse a unique key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"there: “can’t check its unique key inside a private or fileprivate type”. The enclosing type can be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seen from swift-syntax 600 on. With an older swift-syntax the key in such a type compiles and goes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unchecked.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client macro can drop the key there instead of refusing the declaration, when its users declare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same-named types in private scopes on purpose, such as test suites that each declare an event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Login"},{"type":"text","text":". It returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".omitted"},{"type":"text","text":" from LinkerSetsMacroSupport’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKeyInPrivateScope"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static var uniqueKeyInPrivateScope: UniqueKeyInPrivateScope { .omitted }","    \/\/ kind(of:) and uniqueKey(of:attribute:) as before","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record is still written, without the key, so nothing checks it. The macro decides which scopes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are private by the same rule as the refusal, so the two can’t disagree. A key that is empty, or a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey:"},{"type":"text","text":" argument that isn’t a string literal or holds an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation, is refused too ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What is tested where","anchor":"What-is-tested-where"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Format","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Covered by"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs in"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mach-O, macOS"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tests\/CompileFailures"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DuplicateEventNames"},{"type":"text","text":" (an archive read on demand), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DistinctEventNames"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DuplicateKeyInOneModule"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"just test"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ELF, Linux"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same tests, linked with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lld"},{"type":"text","text":"; gold checked by hand"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CI’s Linux Bazel job"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebAssembly"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Checked by hand with the 6.4.3 SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wasm-ld"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UniqueKeyRecordTests"},{"type":"text","text":" reads keyed records"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"just wasi-test","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"COFF, Windows"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Untested: ","type":"text"},{"code":"UniqueKeyRecordTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shows keyed records build and read, but no test links a duplicate","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CI’s Windows workflow","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Bazel tests build their programs with ","type":"text"},{"code":"tools\/link_test.bzl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which links outside Bazel’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"link step so that a link meant to fail doesn’t fail the build. SwiftPM can’t hold such a test: a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"package with a duplicate fails to build as a whole.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Unique keys","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys"},"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"role":"article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article","title":"What the macros refuse"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","title":"Declaring a kind","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","kind":"article","title":"Performance"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:uniqueKey:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declares a record of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" whose value is this declaration’s, and that no other record of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same executable or library may share "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueKey"},{"type":"text","text":" with."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:uniquekey:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetEntry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"kind","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"uniqueKey","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}